# GammaOS zram + block swap fstab for the RG DS Plus (microSD boot).
# Activated by init.rk30board.rc at boot-complete:
#   swapon_all /vendor/etc/fstab_swap.ext${vendor.ext_ram}
# with vendor.ext_ram=1024 and persist.sys.zram_enabled=1 (both in build.prop).
#
# Swap tiers, in priority order (higher swapprio = filled first):
#   1. zram0  (swapprio=2) - lz4-compressed RAM swap, first priority. comp_algorithm
#      lz4 is set in init.rk356x.rc and the 256MB physical cap (zram0 mem_limit) in
#      init.gammaos-io.rc, both before this swapon. disksize 1GB logical.
#   2. swap   (swapprio=1) - the dedicated 2GB block swap partition (GPT label 'swap',
#      /dev/block/by-name/swap). fs_mgr runs mkswap on it at every swapon_all, so it
#      needs no pre-formatting in the image; it is the flash-backed overflow used only
#      once zram is full. `wait` lets the by-name symlink settle if it is not up yet.
#<src>                    <mnt_point>   <type>   <mnt_flags>   <fs_mgr_flags>
/dev/block/zram0          none          swap     defaults      zramsize=1073741824,swapprio=2
/dev/block/by-name/swap   none          swap     defaults      swapprio=1,wait
